2. What is hoisting and what is the Temporal Dead Zone (TDZ)? Explain with examples
>> hoisting is when variables and functions declarations are moved to the top by default before the code is executed,
for example var: js hoists it to the top and gives it the value undefined as an initiating value until the code executes.
functions are hoisted completely with their declarations and the block of code.(wont work until you call the function).
Temporal Dead Zone:let and const data types are hoisted but they dont get initialized at all not even undefined.
if you try to log the variables without initializing console will give an error.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. What are the main differences between == and ===?
>> == is for comparing two values of the same type.
=== is for comparing if the data type AND the value are the same.
